{"id": "85896", "name": "בעיה מילולית – מערכת משוואות למהירות וזמן בנסיעה ברכבת (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>In a railway journey of \\(90km\\) an increase of \\(5\\) kilometers per hour in the speed decreases the time taken by \\(15\\) minutes.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">a</span></div><p>Write a system of equations (one equation per line) to represent this situation using \\(v\\) as the speed of the train and \\(t\\) as the time.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:asys]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:asys]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt1]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">b</span></div><p>Eliminate \\(t\\) from your equations, writing a single equation only in \\(v\\) which represents this situation.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:veqn]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:veqn]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt2]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">c</span></div><p>What is the velocity?</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(v=\\) [[input:ansv]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ansv]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt3]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Write distance = speed × time for the original and for the faster journey (time in hours), eliminate \\(t\\) to get a quadratic equation in \\(v\\), solve it and keep the positive root.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The unknowns and the units</b><br>Let \\(v\\) be the speed of the train, \\(d\\) the distance travelled and \\(t\\) time.  If \\(t\\) is the time (in hours) then \\(15\\) minutes is \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) hour.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The system of equations (part a)</b><br>We need to use the equation \\(d=v\\times t\\) twice. For the original journey we have<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ 90 = v\\times t. \\]</p>For the faster journey we have<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ 90 = (v+5)(t-1/4). \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — Eliminating \\(t\\) (part b)</b><br>From the first equation \\(t=\\dfrac{90}{v}\\). Substituting into the second equation:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ (v+5)\\left(\\frac{90}{v}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)=90 \\]</p>Opening the brackets:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ 90-\\frac{v}{4}+\\frac{450}{v}-\\frac{5}{4}=90 \\]</p>Subtracting \\(90\\) from both sides:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ -\\frac{v}{4}+\\frac{450}{v}-\\frac{5}{4}=0 \\]</p>Multiplying both sides by \\(-4v\\) (here \\(v\\neq 0\\)):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ v^2+5v-1800=0 \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 4 — Solving the quadratic (part c)</b><br>We look for two numbers whose product is \\(-1800\\) and whose sum is \\(5\\): they are \\(45\\) and \\(-40\\). Hence<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ (v+45)(v-40)=0 \\]</p>so \\(v=40\\) or \\(v=-45\\). A speed is positive, so we discard \\(v=-45\\).<p>Check: at \\(40\\) km/h the journey takes \\(\\frac{90}{40}=2.25\\) hours; at \\(45\\) km/h it takes \\(\\frac{90}{45}=2\\) hours, which is \\(15\\) minutes less.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ v=40\\ \\text{km/h} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ansv", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "asys", "type": "textarea", "boxsize": 25, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": false, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "veqn", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "S0:stack_eval_assignments(exdowncase(asys));\n S0:maplist(stack_eqnprepare,S0);\n res:stack_eqncompare(S0,tsys,[v,t]);\n lv:listofvars(exdowncase(asys));", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "res", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-TRUE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "stack_eqncompare(S0,tsys1,[v,t])", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "TIME_UNITS_FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — incorrect.</b> Check the units: the speed is in km per hour, so the time must be in hours, and \\(15\\) minutes is not \\(15\\) hours.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "elementp(vt,setify(lv))", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "MISSING *", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Please use explicit multiplication <tt>v*t</tt>.  STACK thinks your <tt>vt</tt> is a single variable!  Please try again.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — incorrect.</b> Use distance = speed × time, once for the original journey and once for the faster one (time in hours).</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "veqn", "tans": "v^2+5*v-1800=0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "EQN-SIM-TRUE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "EQN-SIM-FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — incorrect.</b> Express \\(t\\) from the first equation and substitute it into the second one.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ansv", "tans": "40", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "EQN-QUD-TRUE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part c — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "EQN-QUD-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "GT", "sans": "0", "tans": "ansv", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "WRD-FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part c — incorrect.</b> A speed must be positive: discard the negative root.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "ALG-FEQ-2-FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part c — incorrect.</b> Solve the quadratic equation from part b.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["ta", "tsys", "tsys1"], "nvariants": 1}